            <ArticleTitle>[Influence of dopamine receptors agonists on clinical and hemodynamic and neurohumoral indicators in hypertensive patients with concomitant obesity].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>67-72</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The article analyzes the results of studying the effects of antihypertensive treatment with the use of agonists dopamine receptors on clinical and hemodynamic and neurohumoral indicators in hypertensive patients with concomitant obesity. Special role is given to the patogenetice factor as dopamine and his relationship with the renin - angiotensin.- aldosterone system, endothelial function, which are aimed at the regulation of blood pressure and obesity formation and progression.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
